 ## 18. Supervisor convergence mechanics
 
-[Recovery and qualification](RECOVERY_AND_QUALIFICATION.md) defines bounded startup/runtime failure handling, durable explicit-stop suppression, ambiguous signed recovery, native full-frame deadlines and per-Agent tick scheduling. [Production release caller](PRODUCTION_RELEASE_CALLER.md) defines the independent signer/caller/owner path and exact-grant historical lookup.
+[Recovery and qualification](RECOVERY_AND_QUALIFICATION.md) defines bounded startup/runtime failure handling, durable explicit-stop suppression, ambiguous signed recovery, native full-frame deadlines and per-Agent tick scheduling. [Concurrency and host qualification](CONCURRENCY_AND_HOST_QUALIFICATION.md) freezes the lock/I/O contract, optimistic read semantics, per-Agent executor migration target and cross-platform SLO gate. [Production release caller](PRODUCTION_RELEASE_CALLER.md) defines the independent signer/caller/owner path and exact-grant historical lookup. [Independent acceptance and release](../../../qualification/runtime-supervisor/INDEPENDENT_ACCEPTANCE.md) defines the external evidence packet, recovery drill and authority separation without self-asserting completion.
 
 The current implementation adds no model, tool or secret-reading authority to Supervisor. Default builds still omit `production-authority`; read-only context/history calls are not execution permits. The source files, focused tests and host qualification executable must be checked on the same committed source and applicable deterministic merge. Historical passes, dirty-worktree runs and control-protocol fixtures are not interchangeable with deployed real-Agentd acceptance.
+
+Ordinary roster/snapshot registry I/O runs outside the Supervisor owner lock, and the process snapshot is cloned in a short critical section. Mutation and production-context paths still revalidate exact durable/control state under the owner lock. The full per-Agent executor/actor split is a separately measured migration target and is not claimed complete by this source candidate.
